1592
01:12:39,540 --> 01:12:43,110
pilots, operational technician,

1593
01:12:43,110 --> 01:12:44,700
maintenance, these are all things

1594
01:12:44,700 --> 01:12:47,350
that will continue to remain, as Cody was mentioning,

1595
01:12:48,396 --> 01:12:50,900
in electric vertical takeoff and landing aircraft,

1596
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:54,720
in autonomous eVTOLs, in autonomous CTOLs.

1597
01:12:54,720 --> 01:12:58,950
Everything in the future of aviation will still require

1598
01:12:58,950 --> 01:13:01,890
many of those jobs that have already been essentially

1599
01:13:01,890 --> 01:13:04,320
perfected by many military folks.

1600
01:13:04,320 --> 01:13:07,410
So to that extent, I think it's,

1601
01:13:07,410 --> 01:13:10,350
now is a perfect opportunity to start thinking about

1602
01:13:10,350 --> 01:13:12,750
how to build that pipeline for apprenticeships.

1603
01:13:12,750 --> 01:13:13,773
So absolutely.

1604
01:13:14,730 --> 01:13:17,264
- I have a critical word of caution.

1605
01:13:17,264 --> 01:13:19,020
So we hired dozens of Skillbridge folks

1606
01:13:19,020 --> 01:13:20,570
through Skillbridge every year,

1607
01:13:21,464 --> 01:13:23,250
and you can, you would expect that we have, you know,

1608
01:13:23,250 --> 01:13:25,113
a huge pipeline of military folks.

1609
01:13:26,340 --> 01:13:28,170
People talk about how challenging the transition

1610
01:13:28,170 --> 01:13:29,610
from military to civilian is

1611
01:13:29,610 --> 01:13:32,940
because it really, really is extremely challenging.

1612
01:13:32,940 --> 01:13:35,580
And the harsh reality is that

1613
01:13:35,580 --> 01:13:38,850
these startup environments are in some cases the worst

1614
01:13:38,850 --> 01:13:42,150
place for folks coming straight out of the military.

1615
01:13:42,150 --> 01:13:45,072
You go from, and I, you know, I've had former,

1616
01:13:45,072 --> 01:13:45,905
I don't have a military background,

1617
01:13:45,905 --> 01:13:47,880
I've had many service members work on my team

1618
01:13:47,880 --> 01:13:50,220
and report to me and in their first few weeks

1619
01:13:50,220 --> 01:13:52,950
and months when they ask me what I want them to do

1620
01:13:52,950 --> 01:13:55,440
and I say, well here's the problem, what do you think?

1621
01:13:55,440 --> 01:13:57,630
Like their brain, like short circuits, right?

1622
01:13:57,630 --> 01:14:01,110
Because they're used to being told like what to do, right?

1623
01:14:01,110 --> 01:14:03,630
And in these egalitarian startup environments,

1624
01:14:03,630 --> 01:14:05,943
that is not how we operate very often.

1625
01:14:06,870 --> 01:14:09,630
And so I think the message there would be, you know,

1626
01:14:09,630 --> 01:14:12,060
I think a lot of times employers think about Skillbridge

1627
01:14:12,060 --> 01:14:14,040
and other programs as like a try it before you buy it,

1628
01:14:14,040 --> 01:14:14,910
let's see if this works.

1629
01:14:14,910 --> 01:14:17,310
And if we like this person and then bring them on full time,

1630
01:14:17,310 --> 01:14:18,930
we should be coaching service members

1631
01:14:18,930 --> 01:14:20,580
to look at it the same way.

1632
01:14:20,580 --> 01:14:23,760
And seize those opportunities to give them exposure

1633
01:14:23,760 --> 01:14:26,310
to these, like, rapidly moving

1634
01:14:26,310 --> 01:14:28,110
highly dynamic environments

1635
01:14:28,110 --> 01:14:30,420
so they can decide if that's really the best first step

1636
01:14:30,420 --> 01:14:33,150
for them coming out of the service.

1637
01:14:33,150 --> 01:14:35,520
And then of course preparing them

1638
01:14:35,520 --> 01:14:37,500
and the employers for actually setting people up

1639
01:14:37,500 --> 01:14:39,240
for success is another huge challenge.

1640
01:14:39,240 --> 01:14:41,340
So I think we have a long way to go

1641
01:14:41,340 --> 01:14:43,470
to better supporting service members,

1642
01:14:43,470 --> 01:14:47,700
primarily in these startup environments, yeah.

1643
01:14:47,700 --> 01:14:48,780
- Nice word of caution.

