- Yeah, now this is an absolutely excellent question

1659
01:15:26,412 --> 01:15:29,480
and it's something that we at Wisk are grappling

1660
01:15:29,480 --> 01:15:30,720
with on a day-to-day basis.

1661
01:15:30,720 --> 01:15:32,430
We're discussing with the FAA,

1662
01:15:32,430 --> 01:15:34,740
we're obviously very, very well in tune

1663
01:15:34,740 --> 01:15:37,230
with all the NASA UTM work that's occurring.

1664
01:15:37,230 --> 01:15:39,150
So air traffic control

1665
01:15:39,150 --> 01:15:42,360
and air traffic management is arguably

1666
01:15:42,360 --> 01:15:46,173
the most critical aspect of this entire system.

1667
01:15:47,280 --> 01:15:50,280
And we've already seen without,

1668
01:15:50,280 --> 01:15:52,830
without these futuristic aircraft in the airspace,

1669
01:15:52,830 --> 01:15:55,383
things are already getting tougher.

1670
01:15:56,220 --> 01:15:59,550
So with all that being said, this is something

1671
01:15:59,550 --> 01:16:01,440
that we're thinking about constantly

1672
01:16:01,440 --> 01:16:04,740
and we are working to understand exactly

1673
01:16:04,740 --> 01:16:06,690
what skills are required,

1674
01:16:06,690 --> 01:16:09,480
how to address that ATC shortage you were mentioning,

1675
01:16:09,480 --> 01:16:12,840
and where like Wisk and really all the players

1676
01:16:12,840 --> 01:16:15,240
in AAM should be positioning themselves

1677
01:16:15,240 --> 01:16:17,250
to make that a reality.

1678
01:16:17,250 --> 01:16:19,920
What we're finding is, as I was mentioning, you know,

1679
01:16:19,920 --> 01:16:24,900
we do remote supervision and that's how we do autonomy.

1680
01:16:24,900 --> 01:16:28,050
Remote supervisors, you know, our multi-vehicle supervisors,

1681
01:16:28,050 --> 01:16:31,860
these folks will be very, very tied at the hip

1682
01:16:31,860 --> 01:16:33,213
to air traffic control.

1683
01:16:34,410 --> 01:16:36,510
And to be totally frank,

1684
01:16:36,510 --> 01:16:40,320
it's going to be a different type of air traffic management

1685
01:16:40,320 --> 01:16:41,400
that we're going to have.

1686
01:16:41,400 --> 01:16:44,850
So we're trying to drum up and brainstorm and test

1687
01:16:44,850 --> 01:16:47,130
and validate what skills

1688
01:16:47,130 --> 01:16:49,800
and what positions will be additionally necessary

1689
01:16:49,800 --> 01:16:51,720
